---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

export const meta = {
  title: '"We have the latest model, why do we need developers?"',
  description:
    'What are you saying? A good AI collaborator is someone who knows their domain first & delegates to AI second? Nah! Go sell potatoes!',
  date: '2026-09-11',
  image: '/ceo.png',
};
---

<Base
  title={meta.title}
  description={meta.description}
  ogType="article">
  <section class="mt-6 max-w-prose md:mt-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl leading-tight font-black tracking-tight md:text-4xl">
      "We have the latest model, why do we need developers?"
    </h1>
    <h2 class="lede mt-3 text-lg font-bold">
      What are you saying? A good AI collaborator is someone who knows their domain first &amp; delegates to AI second?
      Nah! Go sell potatoes!
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-right font-mono text-sm opacity-60">
      <time datetime="2026-09-11">11/09/2026</time>
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-4">
      <p>
        This discussion comes back every generation. Mine got no/low code &amp; the more I tried explaining it wasn't the
        miracle on the box, the harder higher ups clutched their opinion. You just learn to bite your tongue &amp; let it
        pass through their system.
      </p>
      <p>Before us it was RAD tools &amp; SAP. Before them, MS Access &amp; SharePoint ...etc.</p>
      <p>And sure, not just coding, practically every white collar job is solved.</p>
      <p>For who though?</p>
      <p>Vibe coding on localhost:8080 is not the same job as a multi team/service system in prod.</p>
      <p>
        Unless you have unlimited frontier access or a FAANG budget, anyone on a commercial or personal plan has already
        run into the shortcomings. Past a certain usage, which you hit pretty fast in any prod codebase, quality drops
        &amp; shadow rerouting kicks in: fast &amp; cheap localised band aids over band aids output, with little ability
        to step back or plan for consequences.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can mitigate through orchestration, skills &amp; context management. But the only real fix is money:
        continuous billing &amp; tokenmaxing.
      </p>
      <p>
        And that stays a hard constraint as long as major providers are running at a loss, which they will be for a
        while, because energy. Funny enough, Big Energy capital is what's protecting us from Big Tech capital right now.
      </p>
      <p>
        And if this century taught us anything about capital: the end state is always{' '}
        <a
          class="link"
          href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enshittification"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">
          enshittification
        </a>
        . The race for infinite growth on a finite planet leads nowhere else.
      </p>
      <p>
        Once Big AI is done scorching earth, 💩 floodgates will open, prices will reach Elon Musk satellites &amp;
        decision makers will go on a cruise.
      </p>
      <figure class="flex flex-col items-center gap-2 text-center">
        <img
          class="rounded-box border-base-300 border"
          alt="McDonald's CEO"
          decoding="async"
          height="300"
          loading="lazy"
          src="/ceo.png"
          width="300"
        />
        <figcaption class="text-sm opacity-70">
          <a
            class="link"
            href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W6QFxgS8fSA"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            target="_blank">
            McDonald's CEO enjoying his PRODUK
          </a>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
